{"output":"I’ll inspect the search flow and tests, fix the stale-request updates, and run the existing tests without changing them or installing dependencies.\n\nEvery completed request currently updates state, even if a newer search has started. I’ll add a request counter that also advances when the query is cleared, and guard results, errors, and loading updates. The worktree is clean; no AGENTS.md files were found. I’ll use a clean shell to avoid the startup warning.\n\nUpdated src/search/controller.ts so only the latest request can update results, errors, or loading. Clearing the query immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API unchanged.\n\nVerification passed, exit 0: npm test, all 4 tests; node --input-type=module race-condition probe; git diff --check.\n\nNo tests modified or dependencies installed. No blockers.","final_output":"Updated src/search/controller.ts so only the latest request can update results, errors, or loading. Clearing the query immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API unchanged.\n\nVerification passed, exit 0: npm test, all 4 tests; node --input-type=module race-condition probe; git diff --check.\n\nNo tests modified or dependencies installed. No blockers.","exit_code":0,"model":"gpt-6-astra","session_id":"","steps":5,"tool_calls":[{"name":"skill","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"error","action":"run","error":{"category":"command_failed","code":"nonzero_exit"},"command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"git status --short; rg --files -g AGENTS.md -g '!node_modules' -g '!vendor'","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-fair-2tip6hsn/search-1-handwork/repo","exit_code":1,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":207,"stdout_bytes":0,"stderr_bytes":42,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-71e03d47a8c050b1f3b1c97202b3b808.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"npm test && node --input-type=module <<'NODE'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { createSearchController } from './src/search/controller.ts';\nconst items = [{ id: 'latest', title: 'Latest', url: '/' }];\nfor (const outcome of ['resolve', 'reject']) {\n  for (const phase of ['pending', 'completed', 'cleared']) {\n    const requests = [];\n    const c = createSearchController({ search: () => new Promise((resolve, reject) => requests.push({ resolve, reject })) });\n    const old = c.search('same');\n    const current = c.search('same');\n    if (phase === 'completed') { requests[1].resolve(items); await current; }\n    if (phase === 'cleared') await c.search('  ');\n    const before = c.getState();\n    let notifications = 0;\n    const unsubscribe = c.subscribe(() => notifications++);\n    notifications = 0;\n    requests[0][outcome](outcome === 'resolve' ? items : new Error('stale'));\n    await old;\n    assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), before);\n    assert.equal(notifications, 0);\n    unsubscribe();\n    if (phase !== 'completed') { requests[1].resolve(items); await current; }\n    assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), phase === 'cleared'\n      ? { query: '', results: [], loading: false, error: null }\n      : { query: 'same', results: items, loading: false, error: null });\n  }\n}\nconst c = createSearchController({ search: async () => { throw new Error('current'); } });\nawait c.search('query');\nassert.equal(c.getState().error, 'current');\nawait c.search('');\nassert.deepEqual(c.getState(), { query: '', results: [], loading: false, error: null });\nconsole.log('Race-condition probe passed');\nNODE\n git diff --check && git diff --stat && git diff -- src/search/controller.ts","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-fair-2tip6hsn/search-1-handwork/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":377,"stdout_bytes":2230,"stderr_bytes":0,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-